== 7. Performance Optimization

=== 7.1 Large Graph Handling

'''Strategies:'''
* Level-of-detail rendering
* Clustering for overview
* Progressive loading
* WebGL for >1000 nodes

'''Implementation:'''
```javascript
// Cluster nodes by domain
const clusters = d3.group(graph.nodes, d => d.domain);

// Render clusters instead of individual nodes
const clusterNodes = Array.from(clusters, ([key, values]) => ({
  id: key,
  size: values.length,
  confidence: d3.mean(values, d => d.confidence)
}));
```

=== 7.2 Animation Performance

'''Best Practices:'''
* Use requestAnimationFrame
* Limit simultaneous animations
* Debounce interaction handlers
* Use CSS transitions where possible

----
== Conclusion

Knowledge graph visualization transforms BITwiki's semantic data into explorable visual landscapes. By encoding epistemic information visually, users can assess knowledge quality at a glance and navigate complex relationships intuitively.

'''Key Principles:'''
* Preserve epistemic information in visual encoding
* Support multiple layout algorithms for different tasks
* Enable interactive filtering and exploration
* Optimize for performance with large graphs

